---
// Building a path and validating it are specified by different documents.
// Wide drawing for tablets and desktops, a vertical one for phones.
---

<svg class="svg-fig fig-wide" viewBox="0 0 760 278" role="img" aria-labelledby="bv-t bv-d">
  <title id="bv-t">Building a path and validating it are specified by different documents</title>
  <desc id="bv-d">RFC 4158 describes how candidate paths may be built but is informational. RFC 5280 section 6 validates one path it receives already built. Between them nothing fixes how to choose the admissible path, nor which of several is best. PolarisChain works in that gap.</desc>

  <rect class="box" x="10" y="20" width="220" height="164" />
  <text x="24" y="42" class="t-label">RFC 4158</text>
  <text x="24" y="56" class="t-label">INFORMATIONAL</text>
  <text x="24" y="80" class="t-title">Path building</text>
  <text x="24" y="104" class="t-small">Describes the certificate graph and</text>
  <text x="24" y="120" class="t-small">heuristics to order candidates.</text>
  <text x="24" y="136" class="t-small">Its goal is to find a path, not to</text>
  <text x="24" y="152" class="t-small">prefer one over another.</text>

  <path class="edge-dash flow-slow" d="M230 78 C 272 78, 280 102, 308 102" />
  <path class="edge-dash flow-slow" d="M230 102 H308" />
  <path class="edge-dash flow-slow" d="M230 126 C 272 126, 280 102, 308 102" />
  <text x="236" y="160" class="t-tiny">candidate paths</text>

  <rect class="box-dash" x="308" y="20" width="140" height="164" />
  <text x="378" y="80" text-anchor="middle" class="t-accent" style="font-size:30px">?</text>
  <text x="378" y="108" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small">Which one is</text>
  <text x="378" y="123" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small">admissible, and</text>
  <text x="378" y="138" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small">which is best?</text>
  <text x="378" y="166" text-anchor="middle" class="t-tiny">no procedure fixed</text>

  <path class="edge-path" d="M448 102 H500" />
  <text x="474" y="94" text-anchor="middle" class="t-tiny">one path</text>

  <rect class="box" x="500" y="20" width="250" height="164" />
  <text x="514" y="42" class="t-label">RFC 5280 · SECTION 6</text>
  <text x="514" y="56" class="t-label">PROPOSED STANDARD</text>
  <text x="514" y="80" class="t-title">Path validation</text>
  <text x="514" y="104" class="t-small">Input (a) of section 6.1.1:</text>
  <text x="514" y="122" class="t-mono">"a prospective certification path</text>
  <text x="514" y="137" class="t-mono">of length n"</text>
  <text x="514" y="164" class="t-small">Valid or not, by minimum conditions.</text>

  <text x="380" y="208" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small">SCVP (RFC 5055) can ask a server for <tspan class="t-mono">id-swb-pkc-best-cert-path</tspan>, but never defines "best".</text>

  <rect class="box-accent" x="170" y="224" width="420" height="44" />
  <text x="380" y="243" text-anchor="middle" class="t-strong t-accent">PolarisChain: admissible subgraph, then a preference</text>
  <text x="380" y="259" text-anchor="middle" class="t-tiny">constraints decide which paths may exist; the verifier's cost ranks those that remain</text>
</svg>

<svg class="svg-fig fig-narrow" viewBox="0 0 360 500" role="img" aria-labelledby="bvn-t">
  <title id="bvn-t">Building a path and validating it are specified by different documents</title>

  <rect class="box" x="4" y="4" width="352" height="96" />
  <text x="18" y="26" class="t-label">RFC 4158 · INFORMATIONAL</text>
  <text x="18" y="48" class="t-title">Path building</text>
  <text x="18" y="68" class="t-small">Describes the certificate graph and</text>
  <text x="18" y="84" class="t-small">heuristics: it finds a path, prefers none.</text>

  <path class="edge-dash flow-slow" d="M120 100 C 120 120, 180 118, 180 142" />
  <path class="edge-dash flow-slow" d="M180 100 V142" />
  <path class="edge-dash flow-slow" d="M240 100 C 240 120, 180 118, 180 142" />
  <text x="252" y="126" class="t-tiny">candidate paths</text>

  <rect class="box-dash" x="60" y="142" width="240" height="84" />
  <text x="180" y="170" text-anchor="middle" class="t-accent" style="font-size:24px">?</text>
  <text x="180" y="192" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small">Which one is admissible,</text>
  <text x="180" y="208" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small">and which is best?</text>

  <path class="edge-path" d="M180 226 V262" />
  <text x="190" y="248" class="t-tiny">one path</text>

  <rect class="box" x="4" y="262" width="352" height="108" />
  <text x="18" y="284" class="t-label">RFC 5280 · SECTION 6 · PROPOSED STANDARD</text>
  <text x="18" y="306" class="t-title">Path validation</text>
  <text x="18" y="326" class="t-small">Input (a) of section 6.1.1:</text>
  <text x="18" y="344" class="t-mono">"a prospective certification path</text>
  <text x="18" y="360" class="t-mono">of length n"</text>

  <text x="180" y="394" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small">SCVP (RFC 5055) can ask a server for</text>
  <text x="180" y="410" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small"><tspan class="t-mono">id-swb-pkc-best-cert-path</tspan>, but never defines "best".</text>

  <rect class="box-accent" x="4" y="428" width="352" height="64" />
  <text x="180" y="452" text-anchor="middle" class="t-strong t-accent">PolarisChain</text>
  <text x="180" y="470" text-anchor="middle" class="t-tiny">admissible subgraph first, then a preference:</text>
  <text x="180" y="484" text-anchor="middle" class="t-tiny">the verifier's cost ranks the paths that remain</text>
</svg>
